{"name":"Big Cypress","hex":"#b98675","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"big","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Biangai."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of great size, large.","Fat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/big"},{"term":"cypress","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen coniferous tree with flattened shoots bearing small scale-like leaves, whose dark foliage is sometimes associated with mourning, in family Cupressaceae, especially the genera Cupressus and Chamaecyparis."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Cyprus (“type of fabric”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cypress"}],"entries":[{"title":"Big Cypress National Preserve","blocks":[{"text":"Big Cypress National Preserve is a United States national preserve located in South Florida, about 45 miles (72 km) west of Miami on the Atlantic coastal plain. The 720,000-acre (2,900 km2) Big Cypress, along with Big Thicket National Preserve in Texas, became the first national preserves in the United States National Park System when they were established on October 11, 1974. Florida film producer Elam Stoltzfus has featured the preserve and its photographers Niki and Clyde Butcher in several PBS and other documentaries, beginning with the half-hour \"Visions of Florida: the Photographic Art of Clyde Butcher\" produced in 1990."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Big_Cypress_National_Preserve.jpg/330px-Big_Cypress_National_Preserve.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Cypress_National_Preserve","wikidata":"Q478682"},{"title":"Cypress","blocks":[{"text":"Cypress is a common name for species in several genera in the family Cupressaceae. They grow in temperate climates and subtropical regions of Asia, Europe, and North America."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cypress","wikidata":"Q14169641"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Rock_outcroppings_in_the_prairie_north_of_Concho_Billy_Trail%2C_in_Big_Cypress_National_Preserve.JPG/500px-Rock_outcroppings_in_the_prairie_north_of_Concho_Billy_Trail%2C_in_Big_Cypress_National_Preserve.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Rock_outcroppings_in_the_prairie_north_of_Concho_Billy_Trail%2C_in_Big_Cypress_National_Preserve.JPG/1280px-Rock_outcroppings_in_the_prairie_north_of_Concho_Billy_Trail%2C_in_Big_Cypress_National_Preserve.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Rock_outcroppings_in_the_prairie_north_of_Concho_Billy_Trail%2C_in_Big_Cypress_National_Preserve.JPG/500px-Rock_outcroppings_in_the_prairie_north_of_Concho_Billy_Trail%2C_in_Big_Cypress_National_Preserve.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rock outcroppings in the prairie north of Concho Billy Trail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARock_outcroppings_in_the_prairie_north_of_Concho_Billy_Trail%2C_in_Big_Cypress_National_Preserve.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Cottonmouthbc.jpg/500px-Cottonmouthbc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Cottonmouthbc.jpg/500px-Cottonmouthbc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A cottonmouth crosses an off-road vehicle access road in Big Cypress National Preserve.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACottonmouthbc.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Alligator_in_Big_Cypress_National_Preserve.jpg/500px-Alligator_in_Big_Cypress_National_Preserve.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki